Desktop planner table lacked visual indication of the current day, unlike the mobile view which highlights it with a green badge.

## Changes

- **WeeklyPlannerPage.tsx**: Calculate current day index with `useMemo`, apply `th-active-day` class to today's header column
- **index.css**: Style active day header with `var(--primary)` background matching mobile theme

## Implementation

```tsx
const currentDayRotatedIndex = useMemo(() => {
  const today = new Date();
  const currentDayOfWeek = today.getDay();
  return (currentDayOfWeek - firstDayOfWeek + 7) % 7;
}, [firstDayOfWeek]);

// In table header
<th className={`th ${rotatedIdx === currentDayRotatedIndex ? 'th-active-day' : ''}`}>
```

```css
.th-active-day { 
  background: var(--primary); 
  color: white; 
  font-weight: 700; 
}
```

## Result

![Active day indicator](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d95b5e3a-20e7-46ee-8901-94ed8c540780)

Current day column now visually consistent with mobile view. Respects `firstDayOfWeek` rotation setting.

